	('1600ef22-4b77-4d83-a88a-45a7491ce478', 'f9cc9033-3fd4-4f94-bd70-4e584e88df36', 1, 'RISK_PROFILE_V1', 'INITIAL_IMPORT', 'CYBER_SECURITY', 'MANAGE_CONTINUITY', 'BUILD', 'APPROVAL_REQUIRED', 'Business Continuity', 'A business continuity management process must be defined (e.g., Business Continuity Plan) at business process level with adequate measures established and tested (including Disaster Recovery strategy activation if applicable) to ensure business operations during digital solution’s unavailability (e.g., disasters). This process must be maintained and regularly reviewed to ensure its effectiveness and accuracy.', '1. DIG-CO-SOP-0018146-System Life Cycle: https://opella-connect.veevavault.com/ui/#permalink=V190000000IO009
2. QUA-CO-OPE-0093984-Business Continuity Plan for GxP Computerized Systems: https://opella-connect.veevavault.com/ui/#permalink=V190000000EQ023', 'Actionable business continuity plan describing how the business activities will be executed in case of digital solution''s unavailability.', 'When attesting this control, consider the following:

* Is a Business Continuity Plan (BCP) defined at the business process level for this digital solution?
* Does the BCP describe adequate measure to sustain business activities during the solutions'' unavailability (e.g. manual workarounds, alternate processes)?
* For applicable solutions: does the BCP include Disaster Recovery strategy activation steps?
* Is the BCP reviewed and updated on a regular cadence to ensure it remains accurate and effective (e.g. after solution changes, org changes, or prior test findings)?
* Is the BCP readily accessible to the people who would need to execute it during an actual disruption?
* Any digital solution without a maintained, tested BCP - or with a BCP that hasn''t been reviewed within its required cycle - should be treated as non-complaint.', 'OUTCOME_TRIGGERED', '{"groups": [{"conditions": [{"values": ["GXP"], "operator": "IN", "outcomeKey": "GXP_CLASSIFICATION"}]}]}', 'k2V7PtwJFVmlaX60WM6U0JDDu7bYD9mt', '2026-10-23 10:31:20.621', '2026-10-23 10:31:20.621', NULL, NULL, 'CYBERSECURITY', NULL, true, false),
	('00e30d6c-e04f-4262-aee9-c27677830fd3', '7dc4ee96-7e85-4926-ac74-093e861e1e91', 1, 'RISK_PROFILE_V1', 'INITIAL_IMPORT', 'CYBER_SECURITY', 'MANAGE_CONTINUITY', 'BUILD', 'APPROVAL_REQUIRED', 'Alternate Procedures and Continuity Measures', 'Ensure business continuity can be maintained when the digital solution becomes unavailable.', 'DIG-CO-OPE-0293533-Corporate Digital Service Continuity and Disaster Recovery Standard
SECU-CO-MAN-0000101-Business Continuity Management Policy', 'Documented alternate procedures
Business Continuity Plan
Work instructions
Training material
Exercise or test results
Evidence of periodic review and update
Corrective actions arising from continuity exercises', 'When attesting this control, consider the following:

Documentation
Are alternative procedures documented for the affected business activities?
Are the procedures sufficiently detailed for users to execute them without relying on undocumented knowledge?
Are roles and responsibilities clearly defined?
Availability
Are the documented procedures available to the personnel who would need to execute them during a disruption?
Can the procedures be accessed if the digital solution is unavailable?
Training
Have relevant personnel been trained on the alternative procedures?
Is training evidence available?
Testing
Have the alternative procedures been exercised, tested, or used in practice?
Were the exercises documented?
Were lessons learned captured?
Maintenance
Have the procedures been reviewed within the defined review cycle?
Have changes in processes, systems, suppliers, or organization been reflected in the procedures?
Effectiveness
Would the alternative procedures allow the business activity to continue for the expected disruption period?
Are there significant manual dependencies or bottlenecks that could prevent successful execution?
Were any issues identified during testing remediated and tracked to closure?

Non-Compliance Indicators

The control should be considered non-compliant when:

No alternative procedure exists.
Procedures are undocumented.
Procedures have never been tested.
Personnel are unaware of the procedures.
Procedures are outdated or no longer applicable.
Significant deficiencies identified during testing remain unresolved.', 'OUTCOME_TRIGGERED', '{"groups": [{"conditions": [{"values": ["GXP"], "operator": "IN", "outcomeKey": "GXP_CLASSIFICATION"}]}]}', 'k2V7PtwJFVmlaX60WM6U0JDDu7bYD9mt', '2026-10-23 10:31:20.621', '2026-10-23 10:31:20.621', NULL, NULL, 'CYBERSECURITY', NULL, true, false),
	('52efaa54-d952-48ca-8ca2-3ce1da2b7c74', '61f063cc-c93b-447e-ad19-c85687e3b884', 1, 'RISK_PROFILE_V1', 'INITIAL_IMPORT', 'DIGITAL_DATA', 'MANAGE_DELIVERY', 'BUILD', 'APPROVAL_REQUIRED', 'AI Output Evaluation', 'AI outputs shall be evaluated against predefined acceptance criteria before release.', 'https://sanofi.sharepoint.com/sites/ORAIGovernance/SitePages/OR.AI-Opella%20Responsible%20AI.aspx', 'Evaluation Report, UAT Results, Test Evidence', 'Have AI outputs been evaluated before deployment? Have acceptance criteria been defined and approved? Has testing been performed using representative business scenarios? Have evaluation results been documented and reviewed? Are identified issues tracked and resolved before release?', 'OUTCOME_TRIGGERED', '{"groups": [{"conditions": [{"values": ["AI_LIMITED", "AI_HIGH"], "operator": "IN", "outcomeKey": "AI_RISK_CLASSIFICATION"}]}]}', 'k2V7PtwJFVmlaX60WM6U0JDDu7bYD9mt', '2026-10-23 10:31:20.621', '2026-10-23 10:31:20.621', NULL, NULL, 'AI', NULL, true, false),
	('96c211cc-e278-46ec-aa7d-bf3091a64c2c', '4d4a38e3-fa6b-422f-bc9f-390ebdbcf35a', 1, 'RISK_PROFILE_V1', 'INITIAL_IMPORT', 'CYBER_SECURITY', 'MANAGE_CONTINUITY', 'BUILD', 'APPROVAL_REQUIRED', 'Recovery Time Objective Demonstration', 'Vital digital solutions shall demonstrate through testing and documented evidence that recovery can be completed within the approved Recovery Time Objective.', 'DIG-CO-OPE-0293533-Corporate Digital Service Continuity and Disaster Recovery Standard
SECU-CO-MAN-0000101-Business Continuity Management Policy', 'Recovery exercise
Recovery exercise report
Recovery timings documented: Start time, End time, Measured RTO
Data recovery validated
Deviations documented and remediated', 'When attesting this control, consider the following:
Recovery Performance
Has recovery been timed?
Was recovery completed within the approved RTO (Platinum RTO ≤2; Gold RTO ≤ 4 hours)?
Was the approved RPO achieved (≤ 15 mins)?
Were all critical services, data and integrations restored?
