	('56c81f2c-fed5-4268-9b9b-22e28b537280', 'b11d0127-5e35-4680-b5fd-a5c80e7f68ff', 1, 'RISK_PROFILE_V1', 'INITIAL_IMPORT', 'DIGITAL_TECHNOLOGY', 'MANAGE_DELIVERY', 'BUILD', 'APPROVAL_REQUIRED', 'Gather Requirements', 'The digital solution must have a defined set of requirements that describe the functional (i.e., business-process related) and non-functional (e.g., Audit Trail, Electronic Record, Electronic Signature, Data Privacy, Cybersecurity) needs to satisfy the business. All requirements must be specific, measurable, achievable, realistic and testable (SMART).', 'DIG-CO-SOP-0018146-System Life Cycle: https://opella-connect.veevavault.com/ui/#permalink=V190000000IO009', 'The requirements the digital solution must meet, including the list of requirements supporting the business process, as well as the applicable non functional requirements.
E.g.: Epic and user stories in Jira, Requirements in HP ALM, Requirement document in Connect CMS...', 'When attesting this control, consider the following:

* Are both functional (business-process related) and non-functional requirements (e.g. Audit Trail, Electronic Record, Electronic Signature, Data Privacy, Cybersecurity) documented for the digital solution?
* Is each requirement specific, measurable, achievable, realistic, and testable (SMART)?
* Are requirements captured and traceable in the appropriate tool for the solution (e.g. Epics/user stories in JIRA, requirements in HP ALM, requirement document in Connect CMS)?
* Is there evidence requirements were reviewed/approved by the appropriate business and IT stakeholders before design/build began?
* Are requirements complete relative to the business process being supported, with no material gaps identified later in the lifecycle?
* Any digital solution where requirements are missing, non-SMART, or not traceable to a recognized system of record should be treated as noncompliant', 'ALWAYS', NULL, 'k2V7PtwJFVmlaX60WM6U0JDDu7bYD9mt', '2026-10-23 10:31:20.621', '2026-10-23 10:31:20.621', NULL, NULL, 'PRODUCT_PROJECT_DELIVERY', NULL, true, false),
	('5f57ec26-f758-49a1-aeca-e6c01df3e08a', 'cd195fb7-8862-43c3-bcdc-24e1bd3ee273', 1, 'RISK_PROFILE_V1', 'INITIAL_IMPORT', 'DIGITAL_TECHNOLOGY', 'MANAGE_DELIVERY', 'BUILD', 'APPROVAL_REQUIRED', 'Ensure Traceability', 'The digital solution must have traceability by linking requirements to its specifications and testing artifacts.', 'DIG-CO-SOP-0018146-System Life Cycle: https://opella-connect.veevavault.com/ui/#permalink=V190000000IO009', 'Matrix demonstrating traceability between the requirements, specifications and tests.', 'When attesting this control, consider the following: 

* Is a traceability matrix in place linking each requirement to its corresponding specification(s)?
* Does the matrix also link each requirement/specification to its corresponding test artifact (test case/script)?
* Is coverage complete - i.e. can every requirement be traced through to a specification and a test, with no orphaned requirements or untested specifications?
* Is the traceability matrix kept current as requirements, specifications, or test artifacts change throughout the lifecycle?
* Can the matrix be used to demonstrate full lifecycle coverage during an audit or inspection (particularly for GxP solutions)?
* Any digital solution where requirements cannot be traced end-to-end to specifications and tests should be treated as non-compliant.', 'OUTCOME_TRIGGERED', '{"groups": [{"conditions": [{"values": ["GXP"], "operator": "IN", "outcomeKey": "GXP_CLASSIFICATION"}]}]}', 'k2V7PtwJFVmlaX60WM6U0JDDu7bYD9mt', '2026-10-23 10:31:20.621', '2026-10-23 10:31:20.621', NULL, NULL, 'PRODUCT_PROJECT_DELIVERY', NULL, true, false),
	('d02723db-9ed4-4e6d-8395-8918b79b58a0', 'ca198329-d0f9-48e0-9178-333aef2713d1', 1, 'RISK_PROFILE_V1', 'INITIAL_IMPORT', 'DIGITAL_TECHNOLOGY', 'MANAGE_DELIVERY', 'DEPLOY', 'APPROVAL_REQUIRED', 'Authorize for Use', 'A summary of controls execution (as per the defined control strategy) must be documented to authorize the usage of the digital solution. Deviations from the controls strategy must be justified. For unresolved deviations, actions plans must be recorded to monitor their resolutions until closure.', 'DIG-CO-SOP-0018146-System Life Cycle: https://opella-connect.veevavault.com/ui/#permalink=V190000000IO009', 'Summary of the Control/Validation Strategy execution, including at least:
 - all the applicable controls and their achievement''s details
 - deviations from the strategy with associated justification and action plan to remediate them
- the readiness status of the operational & maintenance processes
- decision to authorize the usage of the digital solution
E.g.: Authorization for use, Release report', 'When attesting this control, consider the following:

- Has a summary of controls executed been documented?
- Are all controls defined in the control strategy implemented? If not, are deviations justified?
- For any unresolved deviations, is there an action plan defined with an assigned owner and due date?
- Based on their impact, are there any unresolved deviation that would block the authorization for use?
- Have operational readiness activities been properly executed to ensure the digital solution is ready for operation?
- Has a comprehensive review of control execution, deviations, and operational readiness been conducted to make an informed decision on authorizing the usage of the digital solution?', 'OUTCOME_TRIGGERED', '{"groups": [{"conditions": [{"values": ["GXP"], "operator": "IN", "outcomeKey": "GXP_CLASSIFICATION"}]}]}', 'k2V7PtwJFVmlaX60WM6U0JDDu7bYD9mt', '2026-10-23 10:31:20.621', '2026-10-23 10:31:20.621', NULL, NULL, 'PRODUCT_PROJECT_DELIVERY', NULL, true, false),
	('f09f5f5a-6962-4967-801d-0cbd0ea0e1ef', 'fceaf96c-55f7-4305-bb71-d7f61713c825', 1, 'RISK_PROFILE_V1', 'INITIAL_IMPORT', 'DIGITAL_TECHNOLOGY', 'MANAGE_DELIVERY', 'BUILD', 'SELF_ATTESTATION', 'Execute Digital Properties Process', 'The digital solution identified as digital property must adhere to the Digital Properties process.', 'DFC-QU-GOP-0000613-Life Cycle Management of Digital Properties: https://api-eu.sanofi.com:8443/smartlink/api/qualipso/860315', 'Reference of the digital solution recorded in Digital Property Registry.', 'Reference of the digital solution recorded in Digital Property Registry.', 'ALWAYS', NULL, 'k2V7PtwJFVmlaX60WM6U0JDDu7bYD9mt', '2026-10-23 10:31:20.621', '2026-10-23 10:31:20.621', '{"outcomeKey": "PROPERTY_TYPE", "acceptedValues": ["WEBSITE", "SOCIAL", "MOBILE_APP", "CHATBOT"]}', NULL, NULL, NULL, false, true),
	('f3b2351b-fd27-4d89-9aa2-e9e1badc40d1', '671f1d67-96c2-4d24-a07b-0ed688499887', 1, 'RISK_PROFILE_V1', 'INITIAL_IMPORT', 'DIGITAL_DATA', 'MANAGE_DELIVERY', 'BUILD', 'APPROVAL_REQUIRED', 'AI Risk Assessment', 'The AI solution risk assessment shall be documented and approved before deployment.', 'https://sanofi.sharepoint.com/sites/ORAIGovernance/SitePages/OR.AI-Opella%20Responsible%20AI.aspx', 'Completed AI Risk Assessment, approval record', 'Has an AI risk assessment been completed before deployment? Has the solution been classified according to the applicable AI risk categories? Have significant risks, limitations, and mitigation measures been documented? Has the AI risk assessment been reviewed and approved by the appropriate stakeholders?', 'OUTCOME_TRIGGERED', '{"groups": [{"conditions": [{"values": ["AI_LIMITED", "AI_HIGH"], "operator": "IN", "outcomeKey": "AI_RISK_CLASSIFICATION"}]}]}', 'k2V7PtwJFVmlaX60WM6U0JDDu7bYD9mt', '2026-10-23 10:31:20.621', '2026-10-23 10:31:20.621', NULL, NULL, 'AI', NULL, true, false),
	('c9bb3a1d-a6d1-4e2a-a23e-8d9b511007ce', '62b9c4fe-3506-4ea3-bfcc-f82495a6da00', 1, 'RISK_PROFILE_V1', 'INITIAL_IMPORT', 'DIGITAL_DATA', 'MANAGE_DELIVERY', 'BUILD', 'APPROVAL_REQUIRED', 'AI Documentation', 'The AI solution shall have documented intended purpose, architecture, limitations, risks and usage instructions.', 'https://sanofi.sharepoint.com/sites/ORAIGovernance/SitePages/OR.AI-Opella%20Responsible%20AI.aspx', 'AI Solution Documentation, Architecture Diagram', 'Is the intended purpose of the AI solution documented? Are the architecture, AI models, data sources, knowledge sources, and integrations documented? Are the known limitations, assumptions, and risks documented? Are user instructions and operating procedures available? Is documentation maintained throughout the solution lifecycle?', 'OUTCOME_TRIGGERED', '{"groups": [{"conditions": [{"values": ["AI_LIMITED", "AI_HIGH"], "operator": "IN", "outcomeKey": "AI_RISK_CLASSIFICATION"}]}]}', 'k2V7PtwJFVmlaX60WM6U0JDDu7bYD9mt', '2026-10-23 10:31:20.621', '2026-10-23 10:31:20.621', NULL, NULL, 'AI', NULL, true, false),
	('4a264431-0b0f-492c-a80c-2a2ab55426e8', '3152ad42-2e9e-4435-b7a4-e6dfe653ad57', 1, 'RISK_PROFILE_V1', 'INITIAL_IMPORT', 'DIGITAL_DATA', 'MANAGE_DELIVERY', 'BUILD', 'APPROVAL_REQUIRED', 'AI Human Oversight Design', 'Human oversight mechanisms shall be documented and implemented when required by the AI risk classification.', 'https://sanofi.sharepoint.com/sites/ORAIGovernance/SitePages/OR.AI-Opella%20Responsible%20AI.aspx', 'Design Documentation, User Procedures', 'Are human oversight mechanisms defined and documented? Can users intervene, challenge, approve, or override AI outputs when required? Are roles and responsibilities for oversight clearly defined? Is evidence of human approval or review retained where applicable?', 'OUTCOME_TRIGGERED', '{"groups": [{"conditions": [{"values": ["AI_HIGH"], "operator": "IN", "outcomeKey": "AI_RISK_CLASSIFICATION"}]}]}', 'k2V7PtwJFVmlaX60WM6U0JDDu7bYD9mt', '2026-10-23 10:31:20.621', '2026-10-23 10:31:20.621', NULL, NULL, 'AI', NULL, true, false),
	('ed2b64e1-814f-4ebf-ad7a-92c790278757', '631e3947-386f-4144-97cd-9ffe220a1387', 1, 'RISK_PROFILE_V1', 'INITIAL_IMPORT', 'DIGITAL_QUALITY', 'MANAGE_QUALITY', 'RUN', 'APPROVAL_REQUIRED', 'Records Retention', 'Records generated throughout the digital solution lifecycle (e.g Specifications, Access Request records etc) must be maintained and retained as per the Opella Record Retention Schedule that defines the retention period.', 'DFC-QU-GOP-0000296-Project & System Lifecycle: https://api-eu.sanofi.com:8443/smartlink/api/qualipso/484176', '*Inventory/list of records generated throughout the digital solution lifecycle (e.g Specifications, Access Request records, test evidence, CRs, etc)
*Record retention log or archive index mapping each record type to its defined retention period per the Opella Record Retention Schedule
*Evidence records are stored in a manner that ensures they remain accessible and legible for their full retention period
* Disposal/destruction record for any documents reaching end of retention, showing this was executed per the schedule (not ad hoc)', 'When attesting this control, consider the following:

* Have all record types generated throughout the digital solution lifecycle been identified and mapped to the Opella Record Retention Schedule?
* Are records actually being retained for the period defined in the schedule (not shorter and not definitely without justification)?
* Are records stored in a format/location that keeps them accessible and legible throughout the retention period?
* Where retention periods have lapsed, was disposal handled per the defined process (not informal deletion)?
* Any record type missing a defined retention period, or retained/disposed of outside the schedule, should be treated as non-compliant.', 'OUTCOME_TRIGGERED', '{"groups": [{"conditions": [{"values": ["GXP"], "operator": "IN", "outcomeKey": "GXP_CLASSIFICATION"}]}]}', 'k2V7PtwJFVmlaX60WM6U0JDDu7bYD9mt', '2026-10-23 10:31:20.621', '2026-10-23 10:31:20.621', NULL, 12, 'QUALITY', NULL, true, false),
	('9653efb8-5963-48b3-b289-5f90ac59569a', '934a289e-fa24-491f-a69c-33a9bd6f15ca', 1, 'RISK_PROFILE_V1', 'INITIAL_IMPORT', 'DIGITAL_QUALITY', 'MANAGE_QUALITY', 'RUN', 'APPROVAL_REQUIRED', 'Deviation', 'Detected or potential GxP-related compliance failures impacting a digital solution must be reported as a Quality Event. Each event must be assessed with respect to GxP/Regulatory compliance, Product impact, and Safety, Patients, Data reliability. The associated action plans supporting resolution must be tracked as Corrective Actions and/or Preventive Actions (CAPAs).
 
Note: For Quality Events reported as non-significant deviations, a Corrective Action and/or Preventive Action is not required.', '1. GQCMS-QU-GOP-0000518-Management of Deviations in QualiPSO: https://api-eu.sanofi.com:8443/smartlink/api/qualipso/741670
2. GQCMS-QU-GOP-0000286-Escalation of Quality Events and Management of Quality Alerts: https://api-eu.sanofi.com:8443/smartlink/api/qualipso/470603
3. GQCMS-QU-GOP-0000595-Corrective Action, Preventive Action and Effectiveness Check Management: https://api-eu.sanofi.com:8443/smartlink/api/qualipso/856185', '* Quality Event record documenting the detected or potential GxP-related compliance failure
* Assessment documentation covering GxP/Regulatory compliance impact, Product impact, and Safety/Patients/Data reliability impact
* For significant deviations: CAPA record(s) tracking the associated action plan through to resolution
*For on-significant deviations: documented rationale confirming CAPA was correctly determined not required
* Escalation record, where the Quality Event required escalation per the Management of Quality Alerts process', 'When attesting this control, consider the following:

* Was the GxP-related compliance failure reported as a Quality Event in a timely manner?
* Was the event assessed against all required dimensions - GxP/Regulatory compliance, Product impact, and Safety/Patients/Data reliability?
* For deviations assessed as significant: was a CAPA created and tracked to resolution?
* For deviations assessed as non-significant: is the "CAPA not required" determination documented and justified, not just assumed?
* Was escalation triggered where the event met escalation criteria?
* Any GxP-related compliance failure not reported as a Quality Event, or missing a documented significance assessment, should be treated as non-compliant.', 'OUTCOME_TRIGGERED', '{"groups": [{"conditions": [{"values": ["GXP"], "operator": "IN", "outcomeKey": "GXP_CLASSIFICATION"}]}]}', 'k2V7PtwJFVmlaX60WM6U0JDDu7bYD9mt', '2026-10-23 10:31:20.621', '2026-10-23 10:31:20.621', NULL, 12, 'QUALITY', NULL, true, false),
	('902ec779-ab75-485d-b649-6d514db8ac6f', '547738b3-49f3-4941-9c64-54cb23e30d43', 1, 'RISK_PROFILE_V1', 'INITIAL_IMPORT', 'DIGITAL_QUALITY', 'MANAGE_QUALITY', 'RUN', 'APPROVAL_REQUIRED', 'Corrective Action Preventive Action', 'The remediation of detected or potential failures of a digital  solution to comply with applicable regulatory (e.g. GxP, SOX, CSRD) or Opella requirements  must be tracked and monitored until completion to ensure timely and committed resolution.', 'QUA-CO-SOP-0010049-Management of CAPA and Effectiveness:', '* CAPA record(s) tracking remediation of detected/potential failures against applicable regulatory requirements (GxP, SOX, CSRD) or Opella requirements
* Action plan with defined owner, due date, and remediation steps
* Status tracking evidence showing CAPA progress until completion (not just opened and left open)
* Effectiveness check record confirming the corrective/preventive action actually resolved the underlying issue
* Escalation or overdue - CAPA report, where applicable, showing timely resolution was monitored', 'When attesting this control, consider the following:

* Is every CAPA arising from a detected or potential failure tracked with an assigned owner and due date?
* Is CAPA status monitored and updated until formal completion/closure?
* Was an effectiveness check performed to confirm the corrective/preventive action resolved the root cause (not just closed administratively)?
* Are overdue CAPAs identified and escalated per the defined process?
* Any CAPA left open past its due date without escalation, or closed without an effectiveness check, should be treated as non-compliant.', 'OUTCOME_TRIGGERED', '{"groups": [{"conditions": [{"values": ["GXP"], "operator": "IN", "outcomeKey": "GXP_CLASSIFICATION"}]}]}', 'k2V7PtwJFVmlaX60WM6U0JDDu7bYD9mt', '2026-10-23 10:31:20.621', '2026-10-23 10:31:20.621', NULL, 12, 'QUALITY', NULL, true, false),
	('399bf0cb-4612-4ccb-b598-d966c7427b90', '35c74124-ad69-4891-9cf2-73f91d91971b', 1, 'RISK_PROFILE_V1', 'INITIAL_IMPORT', 'CYBER_SECURITY', 'MANAGE_SECURITY', 'BUILD', 'APPROVAL_REQUIRED', 'China Digital Compliance Requirement', 'If the digital solution is used in China:
It must comply with laws and regulations under China''s cyber security and data security regime.

For digital solutions hosted outside Mainland China: If No personal information or only Technical Personal data is collected from Mainland China, this control is not applicable. Otherwise a China Cross-Border Data Transfer – Personal Information (CBDT-PI) risk review must be included.

For digital solutions hosted in Mainland China: this control must be addressed.', 'QU-GOP-0001332 China Digital Compliance Framework: https://api-eu.sanofi.com:8443/smartlink/api/qualipso/8565258', 'Requestor to contact GRC team - CyberGRC@Opella.com for further instructions', 'Requestor to contact GRC team - CyberGRC@Opella.com for further instructions', 'OUTCOME_TRIGGERED', '{"groups": [{"conditions": [{"values": ["WEBSITE", "MOBILE_APP", "CHATBOT"], "operator": "IN", "outcomeKey": "PROPERTY_TYPE"}, {"values": ["USED_IN_CHINA"], "operator": "IN", "outcomeKey": "TERRITORIAL_COMPLIANCE_EXTENSION"}]}]}', 'k2V7PtwJFVmlaX60WM6U0JDDu7bYD9mt', '2026-10-23 10:31:20.621', '2026-10-23 10:31:20.621', NULL, NULL, 'CYBERSECURITY', NULL, true, false),
	('17e76564-9562-4b8e-aed7-16129a084476', 'ae3a6c15-1b7c-4d72-bbba-5e1b3b8e53c1', 1, 'RISK_PROFILE_V1', 'INITIAL_IMPORT', 'CYBER_SECURITY', 'MANAGE_RISK', 'BUILD', 'APPROVAL_REQUIRED', 'Assess Functional Risk', 'The digital solution''s functions or components must be assessed for potential risks to business, patient safety, product quality, data integrity, and regulatory compliance in the event of a failure. The assessment determines the depth of expected tests or verifications to ensure these risks are controlled.', '1. DIG-CO-SOP-0018146-System Life Cycle: https://opella-connect.veevavault.com/ui/#permalink=V190000000IO009', 'The risk assessment of the digital solution''s functionalities or components, describing the impact in case of failure and level of testing or verification required.
E.g.: Risk issue in JIRA, Risk record in HP ALM, Functional Risk Assessment in Connect CMS...).', 'When attesting this control, consider the following: 

* Has a risk assessment been performed for the digital solution''s functionalities or components, describing the impact in case of failure?
* Does the assessment determine the appropriate level of testing or verification required based on the identified risk?
* Is the risk assessment recorded in the appropriate tool for the solution (eg. Risk issue in Jira, Risk record in HP ALM, Functional Risk Assessment in Connect CMS)?
* Does the assessment cover all functionalities/components in scope, with no material gaps?
* Is there evidence the resulting testing/verification level was actually applied downstream (eg. traceable to the test strategy)?
* Any functionality or component without a documented functional risk assessment, or where the assigned testing rigor doesn''t match the assessed risk, should be treated as non-compliant.', 'OUTCOME_TRIGGERED', '{"groups": [{"conditions": [{"values": ["GXP"], "operator": "IN", "outcomeKey": "GXP_CLASSIFICATION"}]}]}', 'k2V7PtwJFVmlaX60WM6U0JDDu7bYD9mt', '2026-10-23 10:31:20.621', '2026-10-23 10:31:20.621', NULL, NULL, 'CYBERSECURITY', NULL, true, false),
	('a4fec0f0-75a8-40d2-8e0e-9012146b0fe7', '061c96c5-db3b-4596-aa25-f41385f13b6d', 1, 'RISK_PROFILE_V1', 'INITIAL_IMPORT', 'CYBER_SECURITY', 'MANAGE_SECURITY', 'BUILD', 'APPROVAL_REQUIRED', 'Threat Modeling', 'Threats must be identified so that risky scenarios can be understood and mitigated.', 'QU-STD-0000469 Secure Development of Applications: https://api-eu.sanofi.com:8443/smartlink/api/qualipso/910529', 'Cybersecurity Threat assessment describing the cyber security risks which can impact the digital solution and the mitigation plan.', 'Create a Security Architecture Review Intake using the form : https://opella-health.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/CYBSECKB10/pages/557974353/Security+Architecture+Review+Intake', 'OUTCOME_TRIGGERED', '{"groups": [{"conditions": [{"values": ["WEBSITE", "MOBILE_APP", "CHATBOT"], "operator": "IN", "outcomeKey": "PROPERTY_TYPE"}, {"values": ["OPELLA_MANAGED_PLATFORM"], "operator": "IN", "outcomeKey": "PLATFORM_HOSTING"}]}]}', 'k2V7PtwJFVmlaX60WM6U0JDDu7bYD9mt', '2026-10-23 10:31:20.621', '2026-10-23 10:31:20.621', NULL, NULL, 'CYBERSECURITY', NULL, true, false),
	('023531e8-0471-49c6-8484-fe64a836cd58', '6ebf73e1-ce36-45d2-93f3-5010e735736f', 1, 'RISK_PROFILE_V1', 'INITIAL_IMPORT', 'CYBER_SECURITY', 'MANAGE_SECURITY', 'BUILD', 'APPROVAL_REQUIRED', 'Cyber Security Code Scan', 'Vulnerabilities at code level of the digital solution must be identified and remediated. Additionally, if open source dependencies within the code are used then they must be reviewed to ensure proper use.', 'QU-STD-0000469 Secure Development of Applications:  https://api-eu.sanofi.com:8443/smartlink/api/qualipso/910529', 'Result of the code scan with list of vulnerabilities detected and indicating that no critical/high vulnerabilities remains open.', 'When attesting this control, consider the following:

 - Is the code of the digital solution stored into Opella GitHub repository?
 - Has a Cybersecurity code scan been requested and completed, before the release into production, to detect potential vulnerabilities?
 - Is a proof available, including at least: the list of vulnerabilities detected, the scan identifier, the date of the scan, the branch that was scanned, the result of the scan (SCA, SAST...) and name of the person who realized the screenshot and the timestamp?
 - If Critical/High vulnerabilities have been identified, have they been remediated before deployment in Production?

If open-source code is used:
 - Have we ensured compliance usage with the license terms (e.g. use for commercial purposes allowed, number of workstations allowed)?', 'OUTCOME_TRIGGERED', '{"groups": [{"conditions": [{"values": ["WEBSITE", "MOBILE_APP", "CHATBOT"], "operator": "IN", "outcomeKey": "PROPERTY_TYPE"}, {"values": ["EXTERNALLY_MANAGED_PLATFORM"], "operator": "IN", "outcomeKey": "PLATFORM_HOSTING"}]}, {"conditions": [{"values": ["WEBSITE", "MOBILE_APP", "CHATBOT"], "operator": "IN", "outcomeKey": "PROPERTY_TYPE"}, {"values": ["LIKE_EXTERNAL"], "operator": "IN", "outcomeKey": "PLATFORM_TYPE"}]}, {"conditions": [{"values": ["WEBSITE"], "operator": "IN", "outcomeKey": "PROPERTY_TYPE"}, {"values": ["FULLY_MANAGED"], "operator": "IN", "outcomeKey": "PLATFORM_TYPE"}]}]}', 'k2V7PtwJFVmlaX60WM6U0JDDu7bYD9mt', '2026-10-23 10:31:20.621', '2026-10-23 10:31:20.621', '{"outcomeKey": "PLATFORM_TYPE", "acceptedValues": ["FULLY_MANAGED"]}', NULL, 'CYBERSECURITY', NULL, true, false),
	('03c32f91-b27c-4a62-8a4e-5fa948736845', 'be9e314a-4b9b-4b42-bc76-accbe610b6c7', 1, 'RISK_PROFILE_V1', 'INITIAL_IMPORT', 'DIGITAL_TECHNOLOGY', 'MANAGE_SECURITY', 'BUILD', 'APPROVAL_REQUIRED', 'Cloud Security Posture', 'Vulnerabilities of cloud environment of the digital solution must be identified and remediated.', 'DIG-CO-STD-0000031-Systems Security Standard:https://opella-connect.veevavault.com/ui/#permalink=V190000000IV019', 'PRISMA/ SonarQube cloud service monitoring report indicating that no medium or high vulnerabilities are open.', 'PRISMA/ SonarQube cloud service monitoring report indicating that no medium or high vulnerabilities are open.', 'OUTCOME_TRIGGERED', '{"groups": [{"conditions": [{"values": ["WEBSITE", "MOBILE_APP", "CHATBOT"], "operator": "IN", "outcomeKey": "PROPERTY_TYPE"}, {"values": ["EXTERNALLY_MANAGED_PLATFORM"], "operator": "IN", "outcomeKey": "PLATFORM_HOSTING"}]}]}', 'k2V7PtwJFVmlaX60WM6U0JDDu7bYD9mt', '2026-10-23 10:31:20.621', '2026-10-23 10:31:20.621', NULL, NULL, 'INFRASTRUCTURE', NULL, true, false),
	('e77bb6b6-06c4-45ae-a8a4-1e681b2cd5d2', 'aadf54bf-ce93-4cef-a933-a537b4ec4475', 1, 'RISK_PROFILE_V1', 'INITIAL_IMPORT', 'CYBER_SECURITY', 'MANAGE_SECURITY', 'BUILD', 'APPROVAL_REQUIRED', 'Vulnerability Lifecycle Program', 'Infrastructure vulnerability exposure of the digital solution must be monitored all along its lifecycle to ensure it is exempt from known vulnerabilities.', 'DIG-CO-STD-0000031-Systems Security Standard: https://opella-connect.veevavault.com/ui/#permalink=V190000000IV019', 'If a vulnerability is identified through a Qualys scan, the corresponding report will be shared with the application owner, who is responsible for taking the necessary remediation actions within the required timelines.', 'If a vulnerability is identified through a Qualys scan, the corresponding report will be shared with the application owner, who is responsible for taking the necessary remediation actions within the required timelines.', 'OUTCOME_TRIGGERED', '{"groups": [{"conditions": [{"values": ["WEBSITE"], "operator": "IN", "outcomeKey": "PROPERTY_TYPE"}]}]}', 'k2V7PtwJFVmlaX60WM6U0JDDu7bYD9mt', '2026-10-23 10:31:20.621', '2026-10-23 10:31:20.621', '{"outcomeKey": "PLATFORM_TYPE", "acceptedValues": ["FULLY_MANAGED"]}', NULL, 'CYBERSECURITY', NULL, true, false),
	('32e7462f-45a3-4e90-93e3-c7a5fe4dd59f', '0597a0a7-fa5a-4af9-9114-5f078360f96c', 1, 'RISK_PROFILE_V1', 'INITIAL_IMPORT', 'CYBER_SECURITY', 'MANAGE_SECURITY', 'BUILD', 'APPROVAL_REQUIRED', 'Cyber Pentest', 'Attacks must be simulated to identify overall vulnerabilities before releasing the digital solution to production .', 'DIG-CO-STD-0000031-Systems Security Standard: https://opella-connect.veevavault.com/ui/#permalink=V190000000IV019', 'Cyber pentest report summarizing the simulation of the attacks on the digital solution executed and critical risks remediated.', 'Cyber pentest report summarizing the simulation of the attacks on the digital solution executed and critical risks remediated.', 'OUTCOME_TRIGGERED', '{"groups": [{"conditions": [{"values": ["WEBSITE", "MOBILE_APP", "CHATBOT"], "operator": "IN", "outcomeKey": "PROPERTY_TYPE"}, {"values": ["HIGHLY_CONFIDENTIAL"], "operator": "IN", "outcomeKey": "CONFIDENTIALITY_CLASSIFICATION"}]}]}', 'k2V7PtwJFVmlaX60WM6U0JDDu7bYD9mt', '2026-10-23 10:31:20.621', '2026-10-23 10:31:20.621', '{"outcomeKey": "PLATFORM_TYPE", "acceptedValues": ["FULLY_MANAGED"]}', NULL, 'CYBERSECURITY', NULL, true, false),
	('beaa32e4-4a66-47d8-8480-ccecd33b657f', 'd822ebee-5a91-4e81-ba8c-76447f83e11b', 1, 'RISK_PROFILE_V1', 'INITIAL_IMPORT', 'DIGITAL_TECHNOLOGY', 'MANAGE_SECURITY', 'BUILD', 'APPROVAL_REQUIRED', 'Cloud infrastructure code scan', 'Vulnerabilities of cloud infrastructure code of the digital solution must be identified and remediated.', 'DIG-CO-STD-0000031-Systems Security Standard: https://opella-connect.veevavault.com/ui/#permalink=V190000000IV019', 'PRISMA/ SonarQube code scan report from Github repository indicating that no medium or high vulnerabilities are open.', 'PRISMA/ SonarQube code scan report from Github repository indicating that no medium or high vulnerabilities are open.', 'OUTCOME_TRIGGERED', '{"groups": [{"conditions": [{"values": ["WEBSITE", "MOBILE_APP", "CHATBOT"], "operator": "IN", "outcomeKey": "PROPERTY_TYPE"}, {"values": ["EXTERNALLY_MANAGED_PLATFORM"], "operator": "IN", "outcomeKey": "PLATFORM_HOSTING"}]}]}', 'k2V7PtwJFVmlaX60WM6U0JDDu7bYD9mt', '2026-10-23 10:31:20.621', '2026-10-23 10:31:20.621', NULL, NULL, 'INFRASTRUCTURE', NULL, true, false),
	('0949cd7c-1560-48c6-8ffb-31b689442d83', 'f389d049-52ba-4cd9-a1f4-17616cf00b9c', 1, 'RISK_PROFILE_V1', 'INITIAL_IMPORT', 'CYBER_SECURITY', 'MANAGE_SUPPLIER', 'BUILD', 'APPROVAL_REQUIRED', 'Identify Third Party Risk', 'Third Party Risk must be identified during any sourcing activity in order to determine applicable due diligence and contracting actions to be executed prior to final qualification for the Cyber, Data Privacy, and Quality risk domains. A Non-Disclosure Agreement must be signed by both Opella and the 3rd Party to create a confidential relationship if applicable to conduct due diligence activities.', '1. DIG-CO-SOP-0018146-System Life Cycle: https://opella-connect.veevavault.com/ui/#permalink=V190000000IO009
2. For Quality: DFC-QU-GOP-0000498-CS Third Party Quality Management - Sourcing, Contracting, Management and Termination: https://api-eu.sanofi.com:8443/smartlink/api/qualipso/724974
3. For Cyber: DIG-CO-STD-0000020-Third Parties - Contractors Cybersecurity requirements: https://opella-connect.veevavault.com/ui/#permalink=V190000000IY025
4. Procurement Governance: GF-QU-STD-0000419-Procurement Global Operating Standard: https://api-eu.sanofi.com:8443/smartlink/api/qualipso/819585', 'Third Parties risk assessment (e.g Third Party Risk Identification Form completed).', 'All vendors with access to Opella''s network or are critical vendors need to go through the VIRP. During vendor onboarding  in case the vendor does not meet the Opella''s requirements, Risk Acceptance Letter to be signed by the Business', 'OUTCOME_TRIGGERED', '{"groups": [{"conditions": [{"values": ["THIRD_PARTY_ENGAGED"], "operator": "IN", "outcomeKey": "THIRD_PARTY_ENGAGEMENT"}]}]}', 'k2V7PtwJFVmlaX60WM6U0JDDu7bYD9mt', '2026-10-23 10:31:20.621', '2026-10-23 10:31:20.621', NULL, NULL, 'CYBERSECURITY', NULL, true, false),
	('678a5550-f9bd-4876-b675-338460036b48', '292626c1-457a-48e4-b8d1-4cdd71021c82', 1, 'RISK_PROFILE_V1', 'INITIAL_IMPORT', 'CYBER_SECURITY', 'MANAGE_SUPPLIER', 'BUILD', 'APPROVAL_REQUIRED', 'Contract', 'According to a risk based approach based on the third party risk identification process,  the Digital Opella contract Owner (the person requesting and managing the contract process) must ensure that Quality contractual Clauses, Cyber Security measures, and Data Privacy Agreements relevant to the scope of services* are included in a contract with the third party.   

*Note : a Contract, including Master Service Agreement can cover services related to one or several digital solutions.', '1. DFC-QU-GOP-0000498-CS Third Party Quality Management - Sourcing, Contracting, Management and Termination: https://api-eu.sanofi.com:8443/smartlink/api/qualipso/724974 
2. For Cyber: DIG-CO-STD-0000020-Third Parties - Contractors Cybersecurity requirements: https://opella-connect.veevavault.com/ui/#permalink=V190000000IY025', 'Reference of established contract, agreement or Purchase order including proper clauses for each 3rd party used.', 'When attesting this control, consider the following:

For each Third Party providing or supporting the digital solution (SaaS system, On-Premise Software, Middleware, Infrastructure or Platform provider, Managed Services, Outsourced services):

- For Third Party identified as a “High Risk third party”* the control is to be attested in alignment with compliance status found into the High-Risk Third-Party dashboard.
 
Otherwise:
 
For Third Party supporting a GxP  feature / process: 
- Are quality contractual clauses signed by authorized Opella and third party signatories, included into the contract and stored in a contract management system? If not, has a quality contractual clause exemption form been approved by the Contract owner?  

- If the contract is up for renewal by end of the current year, and the contractual clauses have been signed for more than 5 years, is a gap assessment documented and an action plan defined for remediations?
 
For Third-Party that either accesses, stores or manages Opella information, has access to Opella systems, or has privileged access, or supports a vital process: Are the Cyber contractual measures included into the contract?
 
For Third-Party processing personal data: Is the Data Privacy Agreement included into the contract?
 
* A High Risk Third Party is a provider supporting either a Vital activity or handling high risk data (highly sensitive data, sensitive personal data or GxP  / SOX relevant data).', 'OUTCOME_TRIGGERED', '{"groups": [{"conditions": [{"values": ["THIRD_PARTY_ENGAGED"], "operator": "IN", "outcomeKey": "THIRD_PARTY_ENGAGEMENT"}]}]}', 'k2V7PtwJFVmlaX60WM6U0JDDu7bYD9mt', '2026-10-23 10:31:20.621', '2026-10-23 10:31:20.621', NULL, NULL, 'CYBERSECURITY', NULL, true, false),
	('47eb38ee-2766-4d2f-af98-264e19b1b7f7', '71683d28-297d-4101-a40e-4cf7f4d3d942', 1, 'RISK_PROFILE_V1', 'INITIAL_IMPORT', 'CYBER_SECURITY', 'MANAGE_SUPPLIER', 'BUILD', 'APPROVAL_REQUIRED', '3rd Party Assessments', 'According to a risk based approach based on the third party risk identification process, an assessment of the 3rd Party is performed in order to evaluate quality, cyber and data privacy compliance. The results of this assessment are documented; it confirms the 3rd party meets Opella requirements to begin providing the solution or service.   

For SOX digital solutions and associated infrastructure components under the scope of the SOX annual campaign: A yearly independent assessment must be provided for any service outsourced to a Third Party so that compliance assurance is obtained.', '1. DFC-QU-GOP-0000498-CS Third Party Quality Management - Sourcing, Contracting, Management and Termination: https://api-eu.sanofi.com:8443/smartlink/api/qualipso/724974
2. DFC-QU-GOP-0000204-Computerized Systems Third-Party Assessments: https://api-eu.sanofi.com:8443/smartlink/api/qualipso/351770 
3. For Cyber: DIG-CO-STD-0000020-Third Parties - Contractors Cybersecurity requirements: https://opella-connect.veevavault.com/ui/#permalink=V190000000IY025', 'Third party Assessments performed including: third party audit/assessment report, Cyber Security certificates evaluation or completed VIRP, Data Privacy assessment.', 'When attesting this control, consider the following:

For each Third Party providing or supporting the digital solution (SaaS system, On-Premise Software, Middleware, Infrastructure or Platform provider, Managed Services, Outsourced services):
 
For Third Party identified as a “High Risk third party”*, the control is to be attested in alignment with compliance status found into the High-Risk Third-Party dashboard.
 
Otherwise, 
 
- For Quality Assessment:
Based on the Third Party Risk Identification form result for the Third Party, if a Quality Assessment or Quality audit was required, has it been executed and recorded into CONNECT?

- For VIRP (Cyber-Security) Assessment:
If the Third-Party either accesses, stores or manage Opella information, has access to Opella systems, or has privileged access, or supports a vital process: Has a VIRP assessment been completed and registered in the CyberVadis tool?
 
- For Data Privacy Assessment :
If the Third Party processes personal data: Has a Data Privacy assessment been performed in OneTrust?
 
* A High Risk Third Party is a provider supporting either supporting a Vital activity or handling high risk data (highly sensitive data, sensitive personal data or GxP  / SOX relevant data).', 'OUTCOME_TRIGGERED', '{"groups": [{"conditions": [{"values": ["THIRD_PARTY_ENGAGED"], "operator": "IN", "outcomeKey": "THIRD_PARTY_ENGAGEMENT"}]}]}', 'k2V7PtwJFVmlaX60WM6U0JDDu7bYD9mt', '2026-10-23 10:31:20.621', '2026-10-23 10:31:20.621', NULL, NULL, 'CYBERSECURITY', NULL, true, false),
	('c7e4ba55-3260-4f7b-b486-35f1c9e97faa', '93a169aa-e0bb-4285-bb72-ec97fd940a81', 1, 'RISK_PROFILE_V1', 'INITIAL_IMPORT', 'CYBER_SECURITY', 'MANAGE_SUPPLIER', 'RUN', 'APPROVAL_REQUIRED', '3rd Party Monitoring and Termination', 'Relevant 3rd Party failures potentially impacting the data integrity, security, or privacy aspects associated to the digital solution as well as 3rd Party termination must be reported, assessed and addressed in order to minimize impact and restore controls.', '1. DFC-QU-GOP-0000498-CS Third Party Quality Management - Sourcing, Contracting, Management and Termination: https://api-eu.sanofi.com:8443/smartlink/api/qualipso/724974
2. DFC-QU-GOP-0000204-Computerized Systems Third-Party Assessments: https://api-eu.sanofi.com:8443/smartlink/api/qualipso/351770
3. For Cyber: DIG-CO-STD-0000020-Third Parties - Contractors Cybersecurity requirements: https://opella-connect.veevavault.com/ui/#permalink=V190000000IY025', '* Record of 3rd party failure/incident reported, with impact assessment covering data integrity, security, and privacy aspects
* Assessment documentation evaluating the failure''s impact on the digital solution and associated controls. 
* Remediation/corrective action record showing how impact was minimized and controls restored
* For 3rd party termination: documented termination record, including transition/exit plan and confirmation that data handling obligations were met
* For High Risk Third Parties specifically (supporting Vital activities or handling highly sensitive/GxP/SoX-relevant data): evidence of enhanced monitoring commensurate with that risk classification
* Reference to the 3rd party''s classification/risk tier, to confirm the correct level of monitoring rigor was applied', 'When attesting this control, consider the following:

* Has the 3rd party''s risk classification (including High Risk status, if applicable) been correctly identified per the defined criteria?
* Were any 3rd party failures impacting data integrity, security, or privacy reported and assessed in a timely manner?
* Were corrective actions taken to minimize impact and restore affected controls?
* For terminated 3rd parties: was termination executed per the defined process, with data/access appropriately closed out?
* For High Risk Third Parties: is there evidence of monitoring proportionate to that elevated risk (e.g. more frequent reviews, deeper assessments)?

